Implements the immutable structs from #10856.

Minor syntactical hiccup: As is you need to write `new P $ { XYZ }` to create pure structs. This was simply done for testing as I deemed it easier than attempting to figure it out based on name resolution. Example syntax:

```
struct PureStruct {
    x: Int32,
    y: Int32
}

mod PureStruct {
    pub def f(): Unit \ IO = {
        let x = new PureStruct $ {x = 2, y = 4};
        println(x->x);
        println(x->y);
        ()
    }
}
```

Implementation details:
The implementation is not that nice. I didn't want to introduce a mostly duplicated thing so I made the region optional and use that to determine whether something was meant to refer to a pure or non-pure struct.
A struct is deemed either pure or impure based on the presence of a field with modifier `Mutable`. If it is impure it will itself earn the modifier `Mutable`.

